know every single texture and every  single thing was so authentic the show  was filmed under the working title good  faith it was joked that they'd brought  egypt to budapest everything was in  arabic the license plates the t-shirts  everything actor kareem l hakeem attests  it brought me back to being in cairo it  was like a flashback it was so realistic  the smells the smoke the cars the  tuk-tuks even down to the food and the  types of fruit that were on sale in our  marketplace it was really impressive  diob felt that that detail was down to  the newspaper clippings that have been  torn on the floor that's doctor level  precision number four we all need a  friend like the living statue the shots  of stephen talking to the living statue  were filmed in madok square under the  arcadia hotel in central budapest and  fun fact the living statue is credited  as crawley bertrand crawley was a  homeless man living in new york often  working as an informant for the moon  knight number five if hydra's involved  we want nothing to do with it mark wakes  up near a castle in the swiss alps the  scene contains a lot of cgi but the  fortress is inspired by else castle in  germany this isn't the first time this  castle has been used in a marvel series  either hydra's castle to crake from what  if was also modeled after the same  castle it was built in the 12th century  and has stood the test of time because  it's never been destroyed yet shouldn't  say yet number six what do moon knight  and shadow and bone have in common this  place apparently the village was filmed  in the charming town of centendra a few  miles away north of budapest it is a  beautiful little city with narrow alleys  cobblestone streets and pastel colored  buildings number 7. hey look it's  england we remember that place from  spider-man far from home the exterior  shots of england weren't actually shot  in england making parts of the city look  like london required very careful  planning because for one thing the  streets run the opposite way in budapest  the team had to add cars signs a british  red bus because we all know it isn't  london without a double-decker bus and a  ton of taxis the good news was there is  plenty of neoclassical architecture that  worked as the london backdrop and mark  spector lives roughly in the brixton  area of london the set exterior of his  flat is located in downtown budapest  near elizabeth square number eight the  design team needs high praise for this  detail steven's apartment was designed  to give the idea that he lived in an  attic to reflect the pyramids his  apartment has a ton of books historical  artifacts and maps books divide the open  space and his bed is under the loft like  he's in a tomb number 9. worlds apart  and yet similar architecture mark works  at the british museum in london home to  one of the largest collections of  ancient egypt objects outside its own  country the exterior wasn't actually  filmed in england though and instead at  another museum with a similar exterior  the museum of fine arts in budapest  heroes square and both museums are home  to a permanent ancient egyptian art  exhibit the geography in their filming  is just a bit all over the place and  odds are steven wouldn't be traveling by  bus from his flat to his work more  likely buy two number 10. from the  artifacts to the artifacts in the gift  shop the entire egyptian exhibit  interior hall was created from scratch  on a studio set a team of sculptors from  hungary and italy built all the egyptian  statues and columns the interior of the  museum took months to build as well  number eleven you know the road we're  talking about the thrilling car chase  scene on the twisty road was filmed in  osunata in southern slovenia the road is  named bear's guts and has about 20  hairpin turns if you would love to take  a skateboard down that thing turns out  you can it hosts a skateboarding race  called red bull no paws down but be  careful it's one of the most difficult  in the world  number 12 the restaurant staff were just  as excited as those guys in lady and the  [ __ ] going all out with the setup and  everything the set designers dressed up  the restaurant where steven is stood up  by his date or rather where he stood her  up it was designed to look like soho  this beautiful red curved bar is the  troger gastro bistro in budapest  number 13. this is the hottest place on  the list of places to shoot every movie  has shot here did you think we meant the  weather a little fun fact for you wadi  rum in jordan is also known as the  valley of the moon this desert location  is linked to the power of konchu many  other films have been shot in the area  two others oscar isaac was a part of too  including star wars the rise of  skywalker rogue one a star wars story  the live-action remake of aladdin  lawrence of arabia and dune isaac said  if anyone would have told me in the span  of four years i'd be going to do three  different projects in the wadi rum  desert i would have never believed them  that's fair it's a weird thing to tell  somebody it must be a nice place to be  if disney's gone back so much some of  the roads are named after the star wars  shot there too and some of the scenes in  cairo and the desert were filmed in  jordan the wadi rum nature preserve is  popular for a good reason it has some of  the world's most outstanding desert  landscapes number 14. this castle is a  replica but it wasn't made by the studio  built in 1896 in budapest to celebrate  the hungarian conquest of the  carpathians and transylvania in 1895.  this replica of corvin castle in romania  was also featured in the witcher series  and the 2019 movie with will smith  gemini man number 15. sets so authentic  you think they're real beyond sets  beyond meat should expand their market  steven would appreciate the vegan joke  the burial chamber set was built on a  gigantic 4 700 square foot soundstage at  origo studios in budapest because so  many period pieces had been filmed in  hungary the team had access to plenty of  field specific experts who specialized  in things like pottery and hieroglyphics  it took a team of sculptors brought in  from sela's native italy three months  just to create the statues of the  egyptian deities that stand in the  chamber of the gods stella designed the  set to symbolically represent steven as  well her use of water on the set and of  similarly reflective surfaces in some of  the other sets recalls the series themes  of duality and identity  marvel is changing the landscape of tv  and we can't complain about that one bit  the first couple episodes of moon knight  have given us some beautiful shots and  incredible storytelling if you could  visit any of these locations which one  would you choose let us know your  thoughts in the comments and thanks for  hanging out with us here at the things
 

